      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/chemistry/c11-chem/ch8/8.13",
      "title": "8.13 The effect of a change in pressure or volume",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 180,
          "pdf_to": 181,
          "note": "Topic 8.13, printed pages 180-181, with the first Quick Check 8.6."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The effect of change of volume or pressure is not applicable when"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "The system does not involve gaseous components.",
              "The number of moles of reactants and products are equal in gaseous phase homogeneous equilibrium."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "n_{\\text{reactants}} = n_{\\text{products}}",
            "text_alt": "n reactants = n products"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "This effect can only be discussed if the gaseous moles of reactants and products are unequal."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "n_{\\text{reactants}} \\neq n_{\\text{products}}",
            "text_alt": "n reactants ≠ n products"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "In order to explain this effect, let us consider the synthesis of ammonia by Haber’s process."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{N2_{(g)} + 3H2_{(g)} <=> 2NH3_{(g)}}",
            "text_alt": "N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) ⇌ 2NH₃(g)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
